      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s entire architecture was mandated to be Mediterranean Revival, a design choice that still defines its streets today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Gables%2C_Florida",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Venetian Pool, the only pool on the National Register of Historic Places, opened in 1923 and still draws visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Gables%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Biltmore Hotel, opened 1925‑26, remains a landmark and hosts FIFA’s North American headquarters for the 2026 World Cup.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Gables%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Coral Gables adopted its first Historic Preservation Ordinance in 1973, setting a precedent for protecting the city’s historic character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://coralgableschamber.org/a-history-of-coral-gables/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
